            "body": "<details><summary>I have no idea why this error appeared</summary>\n\nHmmm... Strange.\n\n```lua\nvim.env.LAZY_STDPATH = '.repro'\nload(vim.fn.system 'curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/folke/lazy.nvim/main/bootstrap.lua')()\n\n---@diagnostic disable-line: missing-fields\nrequire('lazy.minit').repro {\n  spec = {\n    { 'echasnovski/mini.bracketed', version = false, config = true },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n```lua\nnvim -u repro.lua nofile\n```\n\n```c++\nE5108: Error executing lua vim/_editor.lua:0: nvim_exec2(): Vim(normal):E19: Mark has invalid line number\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_exec2'\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function 'cmd'\n        ...pro/data/nvim/lazy/mini.bracketed/lua/mini/bracketed.lua:1708: in function 'make_jump'\n        ...pro/data/nvim/lazy/mini.bracketed/lua/mini/bracketed.lua:705: in function 'jump'\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n```\n\n</details>",
